[] fight of your live. I would be upset if all I got was a WOP. The wand
[] doesn't allow you to pick what the pile is polymorphed into so I don't
[] think it unbalances the game.

experienced poly-pilers _know_ that a single w.o.p. usually means that
you can generate virtually unlimited poly-spells.  although you can't
pick what the pile is polymorphed into, you can keep trying till you
get what you like.  this is essentially equivalent to wishing and i
personally consider _excessive_ wishing to be unbalancing.  direct
wishes should be, IMO, reduced in number and made more complicated
(but the interface should be friendlier) and indirect wishing (i.e.
poly-piling) should also be made more complicated and interesting.

btw, often by the time you reach the castle level, a good wish is:
a blessed wand of polymorph.  the suggestion that a "sacred" w.o.p.
be placed in the castle is not a bad one, IMO, but i think a "sacred"
wish object is a better idea (that a w.o.p. is a good wish shouldn't
mean that you can't have alternatives).

